.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt REVOKE 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm revoke
.Nd revoke every descriptor of a file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In unistd.h
.Ft int
.Fn revoke "const char *path"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn revoke
takes the file named by
.Fa path
away from every process that has it open.
Each descriptor of it stays allocated, but the file is closed under it, as
at its last
.Xr close 2 :
from then on a
.Xr read 2
of it returns end of file,
.Xr write 2
fails with
.Er EIO ,
.Xr poll 2
reports it hung up, and other operations fail with
.Er EBADF .
Closing it works as usual.
.Pp
For a terminal or another character device, every descriptor of the
device is revoked, however it was opened, the console's included.
.Xr getty 8
and
.Xr login 1
use this to take a terminal from the processes of an earlier session.
.Pp
Any kind of file may be revoked, as on
.Nx ;
.Fx
and
.Ox
take character devices only.
The next
.Xr open 2
of
.Fa path
opens the file afresh.
.Pp
Only the file's owner and the superuser may revoke it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std revoke
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn revoke
fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENOENT
.Fa path
names no file.
.It Bq Er EPERM
The caller is neither the file's owner nor the superuser.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa path
points outside the address space.
.It Bq Er ENAMETOOLONG
.Fa path
is longer than
.Dv PATH_MAX .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr close 2 ,
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr unmount 2
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn revoke
first appeared in
.Bx 4.3 Reno .
In OxideBSD it is system call 590, part of the VFS (OxideBSD-doc
.Pa VFS.md
\(sc4.4).
